        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "gravity-index surface resolution now checks existing metadata",
        "summary": "gravitySurface in gravity-index.ts now accepts existingMetadata and returns its surface field if present, falling back to the agentTemplate.id check otherwise. This preserves previously assigned attribution surfaces during tool calls instead of overwriting them with derived defaults. Scope: packages/agent-runtime/src/tools/handlers/tool/gravity-index.ts. The existing surface value must be a non-empty string to take precedence.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T16:16:02.926Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you use the assistant, it now remembers which version of the product you're signed up for instead of resetting it on every interaction. If your account already had a specific version assigned, that stays in place; otherwise it picks one based on which assistant you're using. You won't see any visible change, but your usage will be correctly counted under the right version going forward.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
