        "v": 5,
        "title": "gravitySurface drops existingMetadata surface fallback",
        "summary": "Refactor `gravitySurface` in `packages/agent-runtime/src/tools/handlers/tool/gravity-index.ts` to derive attribution solely from `agentTemplate.id`. Removes logic checking `existingMetadata.surface`, eliminating the fallback to prior metadata. This simplifies the handler call site by passing only the template object.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T16:15:58.685Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you use the AI assistant through certain products, the system that tracks where your usage comes from will now only look at which version of the assistant template was started at the beginning of this session. It will no longer also try to copy over an older tracking label that might have been saved from before. You wouldn't see this change directly, but if you could look at the background data being recorded for attribution purposes, it would show a single, simpler source label instead of one that could be influenced by leftover prior settings. This adjustment is live now as part of the agent runtime.",
