        "v": 5,
        "title": "Clarify referral tier limits for geo-gated regions",
        "summary": "Updated documentation in `freebuff-referral-tiers.ts` to specify that while users in limited regions can still unlock referral tiers, only standard/free-model limits apply because premium models remain geo-gated. This clarifies the mechanism for tier scaling and perks in restricted areas. The change is isolated to the shared constants file and does not affect core logic or CLI behavior.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T16:16:12.380Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you signed up for the service through a friend's referral in a restricted country, you can still earn higher tiers and unlock watermark-free usage, but you will only get the basic free-model limit instead of the upgraded premium limit because premium models stay blocked in your region. The change only added a short note to the documentation explaining that difference, so nothing about how your account actually works today has changed; the behavior it describes is already how the system treats referral tiers in geo-gated regions.",
